Sparky Stereo OS (ORDER 50 step 4): Jmol's display as a declared 3D area. With Enable 3D (Display menu, on by default, kept in Jmol's own preferences as enable3D) the application runs Jmol's own side-by-side stereo with the preset stereo 5 and perspectiveDepth off, draws each eye's picture at the panel's size and hands both to Stereo KWin in an X11 window of its own inside the frame, declared full side by side with libstereo-declare (patch 0001). The frame, its menus and its status bar stay 2D. Jmol keeps its own stereo angle; a cross-eyed (negative) angle is handed over left eye first.
Display gains "Enable 3D" and "3D display settings..." (opens KScreen); the popup menu's Stereographic submenu (red and cyan, red and blue, red and green, cross-eyed, wall-eyed: output modes) is not offered in the edition's build. Every script command, stereo included, is unchanged.
libjmol-java Depends on libstereo-declare1 (>= 1.7.0) and libx11-6, which the jar loads through JNA at run time.
Maintainer: Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack); Original-Maintainer: Debichem Team; Homepage and Bugs: the edition's.
